<DocsLayout title="MyPaaS documentation" description="Install, deploy, configure, operate, and automate MyPaaS on a single Linux VM.">
<section><p class="overline">Overview</p><h2>What MyPaaS is</h2><p>MyPaaS is a self-hosted deployment control plane for one Linux server. It accepts Git repositories and public OCI images, serves static releases directly through Caddy, and operates container workloads through one Docker-compatible command/socket contract. Fresh supported hosts are Podman-first with rootful Podman as the installer default; Docker Engine remains an explicit compatibility mode.</p><aside class="note"><p>These public docs describe current behavior on <code>main</code>. Roadmap and historical requirements are not presented as available features.</p></aside></section>
